| **1894**          | Founding of Congregation Schaarai Zedek, Tampa's oldest Jewish congregation.                                                       |
| **1917**          | Dedication of the first permanent Schaarai Zedek synagogue building in Tampa.                                                      |
| **1924**          | Establishment of Rodeph Sholom Congregation, serving Tampa's growing Orthodox Jewish community.                                    |
| **1930s–1940s**   | Jewish residents play prominent roles in Tampa's business, civic, and charitable development.                                      |
| **1948**          | Tampa's Jewish community organizes support and fundraising efforts following the establishment of the State of Israel.             |
| **1950s–1970s**   | Rapid growth of Tampa's Jewish population as families move into new neighborhoods and suburbs.                                     |
| **1980s**         | Expansion of Jewish educational, cultural, and community institutions throughout the Tampa Bay area.                               |
| **1990**          | Opening of the Tampa Jewish Community Center's expanded facilities, reflecting community growth.                                   |
| **2000s–Present** | Continued growth of Jewish life in Tampa, including synagogues, schools, cultural organizations, and Holocaust education programs. |

